course: dictionary
lesson: 6774
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word opposition has more than one meaning. The sentence around it tells you which meaning the writer wants. Read the words near it, then ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «There was strong opposition to the new rule, and many families spoke out against it.» Here opposition means strong disagreement with a plan or idea. Check it: "there was strong disagreement to the new rule" makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «At Prime Minister's Questions, MPs question the prime minister, the opposition challenges the government, and the Speaker keeps order.» Here the opposition means the parties in Parliament that are not in the government. Their job is to challenge it. The clue is the word government, which tells you it means the other side.
explain: In a game, «the opposition» means the other team, the one you are playing against. So when you meet a word you know, check whether its meaning fits the sentence. If it does not, look for a different meaning.
fact: Opposition means strong disagreement with a plan or idea, often shown by speaking or acting against it.
fact: In sport, the opposition is the team or player you are playing against.
fact: In politics, the Opposition means the parties in Parliament that are not in government, especially the biggest one.
fact: «In opposition to» means against something.
fact: «The opposition is the parties not in government; their job is to challenge it.»
exercise: At Prime Minister's Questions, what is the job of the opposition? | To cook lunch for the Prime Minister | To sit silently at the back | To watch the football | *To challenge the government
exercise: Many people showed opposition to the new rule. What does opposition mean here? | Strong support for the rule | A long walk home | *Strong disagreement with the rule | Winning a race
exercise: Which sentence uses opposition to mean the other team? | We were in opposition to the idea. | There was opposition to the plan at the meeting. | *The opposition scored twice before half-time. | The opposition in Parliament asked a question.
test: Which best describes the Opposition in Parliament? | The Prime Minister's family | *The parties not in government, especially the biggest one | The people who count the votes | The team that wins every match
test: Which phrase means the same as "against"? | in addition to | in agreement with | in favour of | *in opposition to
exam: Read «MPs question the prime minister, the opposition challenges the government.» What does opposition mean? | A kind of food | Waiting in a queue | Agreement with everything | *The parties not in government
